    "turn_idx": 34,
    "turn_text": "again and that you know that was a while back. But I do think, so to answer your questions more directly, Alex, I do think I have the personality and the stamina to really reach out and figure out who those people are, who maybe, you know, aren't going to come with me to pass a Green New Deal or to pass, you know, Medicare for all. But what are some of the things that we can where I can meet them where they are, they can meet me where I am, and where we can mutually benefit Americans all around, right? And not worry about right now who's getting credit for this, but just really delivering for people. And I feel like if that's what all of us continue to kind of focus on is how do we deliver for people who I feel like frequently want the same thing, right? It's just like, how do we get there? And I do think I have that kind of personality to kind of be that kind of voice in Congress. So I'm excited to kind of take it. And I feel like I've been that role in that person in the state legislature. And I feel like I can do the same thing. And like you said, knowing that it can be frustrating and it could be gridlock. But I think there are smaller things that can be done and certainly delivering for this new congressional district, where I think agriculture is going to be big. And I think working families still have issues that they care about. And I think I can be that voice.",
