    "turn_text": "So that is a good transition to the next portion of our conversation where we want to ask about specific policy issues. So to start with something that I think is actually on a lot of voters mind right now is there's a New York Times article and I'm guessing you probably agree with this framing where they basically said whether it's pro choice advocates or pro life advocates. Virtually everyone agrees that the Supreme Court is likely to strike down Roe v Wade and create new precedent of some kind and likely the likely outcome is that the decision about abortion access gets referred to the states. Before we talk about policy or Congress's role, I know you've been working on reproductive healthcare access for a long time. What does America look like in a post-row world where the decision is left to the states? What are the challenges of that kind of a model?",
