  {
    "episode_id": 89059,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/9/89059.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 107,
    "turn_text": "No, again, you know, it's, you know, the house majority pack is a super pack. And so we don't know, you know, who their donors are. And yeah, so, you know, there's been, you know, I think speculation, but I mean, really what it comes back to, I think is who really is behind Carrick Flynn's donations, right? And we know that Sam Bingman freed is a cryptocurrency billionaire. He's backing. you know, our crypto candidate. And really, I think there are a lot of questions about what he, what his motivations are. And, you know, and he's, you know, I think set on the record to Politico, he wants to influence a couple of these races around the nation in order to help influence what cryptocurrency regulation looks like, right? So yeah, so what House Majority Pack did and why they did it when there are, you know, well, like you said, nine candidates here and four women and the three women of color are the only ones who have held elected positions. This feels like a weird place for the House Majority Pack and truly a slap in the face to voters and volunteers for the House Majority Pack to put their thumb on the scale.",
